## DEFINITION
Clustal Omega is a multiple sequence alignment (MSA) tool used to align DNA, RNA, or protein sequences and identify conserved regions
and evolutionary relationships.

## PURPOSE
- Perform multiple sequence alignment.
- Identify conserved regions.
- Study evolutionary relationships.
- Prepare sequences for phylogenetic analysis.

## WORKFLOW
- Upload input sequences.
- Perform multiple sequence alignment.
- Generate alignment.
- Download and analyze results.

## APPLICATIONS
- Multiple sequence alignment.
- Phylogenetic analysis.
- Protein family analysis.
- Conserved motif identification.

## OUTPUT FILES
- Alignment file (.aln)
- FASTA alignment (.fasta)
- Clustal format (.clustal/.aln)
- Phylogenetic guide tree (.dnd/.nwk)

## FILES TO UPLOAD
- FASTA (.fasta, .fa)
- Text (.txt) with FASTA-formatted sequences
- Protein sequences
- DNA/RNA sequences

## IMPORTANT POINTS
- Supports DNA, RNA, and protein sequences.
- Produces high-quality multiple sequence alignments.
- Generates a guide tree for phylogenetic analysis.
- Commonly used before phylogenetic tree construction.
